@@ -24,6 +24,29 @@ After making changes to this gem, you need to update Fizzy to pick up the change
 BUNDLE_GEMFILE=Gemfile.saas bundle update --conservative fizzy-saas
 ```
 
+## Billing
+
+Three plans, defined in `saas/app/models/plan.rb`:
+
+| Plan | Price | Cards | Storage |
+|------|-------|-------|---------|
+| Free | $0 | 1,000 | 1 GB |
+| Unlimited | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB |
+
+Stripe hosts the checkout and the customer portal, and posts subscription changes to
+`/stripe/webhooks`, where they are mirrored onto `Account::Subscription`. The two paid
+plans are matched to their Stripe prices through `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` and
+`STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`.
+
+An account that has used all its cards can still draft. Publishing and creating through
+the API are refused, and the create buttons turn into an upgrade pitch. The last hundred
+cards count down in the app.
+
+Support tools live at `/admin/accounts`: comp an account, which grants the paid features
+without charging for it, or override an account card count and bytes used to see what it
+sees. Both are undone from the same page.
+
